 34S  c  1976Me03: a 31-MeV 12C beam was provided from the MP Tandem Van de Graaff accelerator at the Nuclear Research Center in Strasbourg, France. The target was a 100-ug/cm2 self-supporting {+27}Al target. A 7-mg/cm2 Au foil was used as the stopper for recoiling ions. The beam was stopped in a thick Ta foil behind the stopper. |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. 
